<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">451 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">451 CE in world history: 14 events and 1 death. 160 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/435">435 CE</a><a href="/years/439">439 CE</a><a href="/years/447">447 CE</a><a href="/years/450">450 CE</a><a href="/years/451" aria-current="page">451 CE</a><a href="/years/452">452 CE</a><a href="/years/453">453 CE</a><a href="/years/454">454 CE</a><a href="/years/455">455 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/attila" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/attila.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-7">7 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Attila and his army capture Metz</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Marching west into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-belgica">Belgica</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gepids">Gepids</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoths</a>, Alans and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metz">Metz</a>, killing most of its people and burning the town; he also took Strasbourg. Aëtius and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> later checked him at the Catalaunian Plains.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/hunnic-empire">Hunnic Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metz">Metz</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-avarayr" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-avarayr.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-26">26 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Sasanian army defeats Armenian rebels at Avarayr</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">On the Avarayr plain, the army of the Sasanian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazdegerd-ii">Yazdegerd II</a>, who sought to impose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zoroastrianism">Zoroastrianism</a>, defeated Armenian rebels led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardan-mamikonian">Vardan Mamikonian</a>, who was killed. The victory proved pyrrhic, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a> were allowed to keep practising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> freely.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-avarayr">Battle of Avarayr</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/visigoths.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-20">20 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Aetius checks Attila at the Catalaunian Plains</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A coalition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Aetius</a> fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> to a halt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, on a date traditionally given as 20 June. Attila withdrew, and invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> the following year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-8">8 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Council of Chalcedon opens</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishops</a> summoned by Emperor Marcian met at Chalcedon, across the Bosporus from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. Its definition of Christ as one person in two natures became orthodoxy in the West and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> but split the eastern churches.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-catalaunian-plains" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-catalaunian-plains.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-catalaunian-plains">Battle of the Catalaunian Plains</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of the Catalaunian Plains was fought in 451 in north-eastern Gaul between the Hunnic army of Attila and a coalition led by the Roman general Aetius and the Visigothic king Theodoric I.</p></div></li></ol></section>
